{
  "id": "m60l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Cola de prioridad",
    "en": "Priority queue"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Atender por prioridad"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Si guardas tuplas `(prioridad, dato)` en un heap, `heappop` te devuelve siempre la de menor prioridad (número más bajo). Es una **cola de prioridad** lista para usar."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import heapq",
          "h = [(2, 'b'), (1, 'a'), (3, 'c')]",
          "heapq.heapify(h)",
          "print(heapq.heappop(h))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "(1, 'a')"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "`heapify` convierte una lista en heap en O(n), más rápido que insertar uno a uno."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Serving by priority"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "If you store `(priority, item)` tuples in a heap, `heappop` always returns the one with the lowest priority (smallest number). It's a ready-made **priority queue**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import heapq",
          "h = [(2, 'b'), (1, 'a'), (3, 'c')]",
          "heapq.heapify(h)",
          "print(heapq.heappop(h))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "(1, 'a')"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "`heapify` turns a list into a heap in O(n), faster than inserting one by one."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m60l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `n_mayores(nums, n)` que devuelva los n valores más grandes (usa heapq.nlargest).",
        "en": "Define `n_mayores(nums, n)` returning the n largest values (use heapq.nlargest)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def n_mayores(nums, n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def n_mayores(nums, n):",
        "    return heapq.nlargest(n, nums)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "heapq.nlargest(n, nums)."
        ],
        "en": [
          "heapq.nlargest(n, nums)."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "n_mayores",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  5,
                  1,
                  8,
                  3
                ],
                2
              ],
              "expected": [
                8,
                5
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  7
                ],
                1
              ],
              "expected": [
                7
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m60l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `orden_prioridad(tareas)`: tareas es una lista de [prioridad, nombre]; devuelve los nombres por prioridad ascendente (heap).",
        "en": "Define `orden_prioridad(tareas)`: tareas is a list of [priority, name]; return names by ascending priority (heap)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def orden_prioridad(tareas):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import heapq",
        "",
        "def orden_prioridad(tareas):",
        "    h = [tuple(x) for x in tareas]",
        "    heapq.heapify(h)",
        "    return [heapq.heappop(h)[1] for _ in range(len(h))]"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Convierte a tuplas, heapify y saca el nombre (índice 1) en orden."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Convert to tuples, heapify and pop the name (index 1) in order."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "orden_prioridad",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    2,
                    "b"
                  ],
                  [
                    1,
                    "a"
                  ],
                  [
                    3,
                    "c"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                "a",
                "b",
                "c"
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  [
                    5,
                    "x"
                  ]
                ]
              ],
              "expected": [
                "x"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}